 {"id":"fabro-44b6","title":"gofib: add -format csv output mode","status":"closed","type":"feature","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-08-27T13:21:49.662Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-27T13:27:57.332Z","description":"Extend the -format family with a fifth mode csv.\n\nRequirements:\n- 'gofib -format csv' emits one CSV record per line: '<index>,<fib>' (index decimal int, fib value unquoted string; values contain no commas/quotes so no quoting rules are needed). No header line — one-record-per-line symmetry with JSON mode.\n- Combines with -n, -start, -limit exactly like every other mode (e.g. 'gofib -format csv -n 5' prints 5 records; '-start 10 -limit 12' prints indices 10..12).\n- -seed lookup mode in csv prints the single record '<index>,<fib>' for the requested index.\n- -sum in csv mode prints exactly one record 'sum,<start>,<last>,<total>' (mirrors JSON mode's index_range+sum structure in CSV grammar).\n- parseMode accepts 'csv'; the invalid-format error message names all five modes: text, json, pretty, table, csv. modeName returns 'csv'.\n- There is NO -csv shortcut flag; only -format selects it. Shortcut agreement rules (-json/-pretty with explicit -format) are unchanged.\n- Extend fib_test.go following the existing patterns: table-driven tests for csv default, csv+-n, csv+-start+-limit, csv+-seed, csv+-sum, and csv in TestRunFormatModes/ShortcutEquivalence/RejectsInvalidFormat where the mode lists appear.\n- No external dependencies (stdlib only; encoding/csv allowed but fmt is sufficient).\n- Update README.md flag reference: csv under -format with examples.\n\nDone when 'gofib -format csv -n 3' prints '1,1', '2,1', '3,2', the invalid-format error lists csv, all new tests pass, and 'just qualitygate' is green.","labels":["ready-for-agent"],"closedAt":"2026-08-27T13:27:57.332Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-28e8","title":"gofib: consolidate flag parsing and validation into an options struct","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-08-27T13:21:49.757Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-27T13:36:00.606Z","description":"Refactor: behavior-preserving. run() currently takes 10 positional parameters and validates flags inline in scattered branches; main() owns flag parsing.\n\nRequirements:\n- Introduce 'type options struct' holding every flag value (n, start, limit, seed, format, json, pretty, version, sum) and 'parseOptions(args []string) (options, error)' that owns flag.Parse AND all validation currently inside run() (invalid n/start/limit/seed, seed+sum conflict, format validity, format-vs-shortcut disagreement) plus -o output path when it exists (see follow-up seed; design parseOptions so adding a field is the only change needed).\n- run becomes 'run(w io.Writer, opts options) error' with no inline flag validation — parseOptions is the single rejection point; error strings stay byte-identical (existing tests pin them).\n- main shrinks to: opts, err := parseOptions(os.Args[1:]); on error print to stderr and exit 1; else resolve writer, run.\n- New table-driven TestParseOptionsInvalid covering EVERY rejection case with its exact error message (n=0, n=-1, start<0, limit<0, seed<0, seed+sum, bad format value, format=json + pretty=true disagreement, format=pretty + json=true disagreement) and TestParseOptionsDefaults pinning defaults (n=100, start=0, limit=0, seed=0, format=\"\", all bools false).\n- The -version ignore-invalid semantics (version short-circuits before validation) must be preserved: parseOptions returns the version flag without validating the rest; pin it with a test.\n- No behavior change: all existing tests pass unmodified except call-site adaptation to the new run signature (table constructors updated, assertions untouched).\n- No external dependencies. 'just qualitygate' green.\n\nDone when run() has no flag validation, parseOptions is the only validator, the new tables cover every rejection, and the full suite is green.","labels":["ready-for-agent"],"closedAt":"2026-08-27T13:36:00.606Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-c295","title":"gofib: add -o flag to write output to a file","status":"closed","type":"feature","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-08-27T13:21:49.847Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-27T13:40:34.370Z","description":"Add '-o <path>' (default empty = stdout, behavior unchanged).\n\nRequirements:\n- When -o is set, ALL output goes to the file: every format mode (text/json/pretty/table/csv), -sum output, and -version output. Uniform rule, no mode exceptions.\n- File semantics: create or truncate (os.Create). On success print NOTHING to stdout, exit 0.\n- Failure to open (unwritable directory, permission) exits 1 with 'gofib: cannot open <path>: <os error>' on stderr and no stdout output.\n- Usage text explains the default (empty = stdout).\n- Structure: keep run(w io.Writer, opts) unchanged; resolve the writer in main (or a small resolveOutput(path) (io.WriteCloser, error) helper added next to parseOptions). Tests: -o with a temp dir file produces byte-identical content to the equivalent stdout invocation (table across text, json, csv modes); -o to a non-creatable path returns the error; -version -o writes the version line into the file.\n- No external dependencies. 'just qualitygate' green.\n- Update README.md flag reference: -o with examples.\n\nDone when 'gofib -o out.txt -n 3' writes 3 lines to out.txt, stdout stays empty, exit code 0, tests cover the modes and error path, and the gate is green.","labels":["ready-for-agent"],"closedAt":"2026-08-27T13:40:34.370Z"}
-{"id":"fabro-7e44","title":"develop: scope the evidence diff per seed, not per run base","status":"open","type":"feature","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-08-27T15:14:04.646Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-27T15:14:04.646Z","description":"From the improve review of run 01M11P68SHFS165HP9ATK6094V (recommendation 1, highest impact).\n\nProblem: evidence.nu diffs seed-work files against the RUN base, so the capture accumulates every closed seed's hunks: 21.8 KB -> 53.4 KB -> 58.1 KB across the three loops. Reviewers then page through closed-seed hunks in a blob ref (reviewer@2/@3 journals), burning 30-60 s and tool detours per review — the main 'Verification blocked' trigger.\n\nRequirements:\n- Anchor the evidence diff at the commit where the CURRENT seed was claimed (the per-seed checkpoint commit exists in the run branch history; the engine already creates a commit per stage visit).\n- The capture header must name the diff base (seed-claim SHA) so the reviewer can attribute scope mechanically.\n- Integrity header and seed-work file list stay run-scoped (they are small); only the diff scope changes.\n- Keep -U3 context (fabro applied 2026-08-27).\n- Expected: captures stay ~15-25 KB regardless of loop count; no blob demotion on single-seed captures.\n\nDone when a 2-seed develop run's second evidence capture contains ONLY the second seed's diff hunks and the reviewer journal records context-only approval.","labels":["ready-for-agent"]}
+{"id":"fabro-7e44","title":"develop: scope the evidence diff per seed, not per run base","status":"in_progress","type":"feature","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-08-27T15:14:04.646Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-01T13:01:05.643Z","description":"From the improve review of run 01M11P68SHFS165HP9ATK6094V (recommendation 1, highest impact).\n\nProblem: evidence.nu diffs seed-work files against the RUN base, so the capture accumulates every closed seed's hunks: 21.8 KB -> 53.4 KB -> 58.1 KB across the three loops. Reviewers then page through closed-seed hunks in a blob ref (reviewer@2/@3 journals), burning 30-60 s and tool detours per review — the main 'Verification blocked' trigger.\n\nRequirements:\n- Anchor the evidence diff at the commit where the CURRENT seed was claimed (the per-seed checkpoint commit exists in the run branch history; the engine already creates a commit per stage visit).\n- The capture header must name the diff base (seed-claim SHA) so the reviewer can attribute scope mechanically.\n- Integrity header and seed-work file list stay run-scoped (they are small); only the diff scope changes.\n- Keep -U3 context (fabro applied 2026-08-27).\n- Expected: captures stay ~15-25 KB regardless of loop count; no blob demotion on single-seed captures.\n\nDone when a 2-seed develop run's second evidence capture contains ONLY the second seed's diff hunks and the reviewer journal records context-only approval.","labels":["ready-for-agent"]}
 {"id":"fabro-f831","title":"develop: make lesson capture enforceable in the implementer outcome contract","status":"open","type":"task","priority":3,"createdAt":"2026-08-27T15:14:04.738Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-27T15:14:04.738Z","description":"From the improve review of run 01M11P68SHFS165HP9ATK6094V (recommendation 5).\n\nProblem: implementer.md step 6 asks for 'ml record' when something durable surfaced, but it is not part of the required outcome JSON — implementer@1 recorded a textbook lesson in the journal, yet no .mulch/ change appears in any checkpoint diff. The lesson dies with the run journal.\n\nRequirements:\n- Add to the 'succeeded' outcome checklist in prompts/implementer.md one line: either an 'ml record' was run (name the mx-id) or an explicit 'nothing durable — skipped'.\n- Mirror the journal-contract pattern (required keys, never optional silence).\n- Keep it honest: skipping is a valid answer; only silence is a violation.\n\nDone when the next develop run's implementer summaries all carry the record-or-skip line and at least one ml record lands when a real lesson exists.","labels":["ready-for-agent"]}
